OL,3,GNEWSABridge safe for another 50 years,
OL,4,Acouncillors told
OL,5,
OL,6,FCouncillors have been reassured a
OL,7,Fbridge is safe to remain in place for
OL,8,Fanother 50 years, after the demolition
OL,9,Fof a nearby flyover raised questions
OL,10,Fabout its structural integrity.
OL,12,FGateshead Council's corporate resources
OL,13,Fscrutiny committee was told there were
OL,14,Fno plans to decommission the Redheugh
OL,15,FBridge, and that officers were
OL,16,Fsatisfied it was far away from the end
OL,17,Fof its useful life.
